#: ../../reading-guide.md:81 c786d73bf14f472c84bb9ce3a5188b33
msgid ""
"The same principle applies within the mathematics. The statement of a model "
"and the meaning of its result belong on the first pass. Proof-oriented "
"detail, duality, and sensitivity to maintained assumptions reward a slower "
"return once the economic question is settled."
msgstr "同一原则也适用于数学内容。模型的表述及其结果的含义应在第一遍掌握；等经济问题已经厘清，再放慢速度研究证明细节、对偶关系和结果对既定假设的敏感程度，会有更大收获。"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:86 000e89b560144b2e87a075462e6efd50
msgid "If You Are Conducting an Empirical Study"
msgstr "如果你正在开展经验研究"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:88 26fa61cb08264682a1efbe9b11c603e8
msgid ""
"Readers who already have data and a research question need not proceed "
"linearly. Use the study-design chapter to audit the unit boundary, decision "
"horizon, managerial control, measurement definitions, and peer-eligibility "
"rule. Identifying inputs, desirable outputs, and undesirable outputs is "
"necessary but not sufficient: a contextual condition is not automatically a "
"resource, an internal handoff is not automatically a final output, and a "
"quantity fixed over one planning horizon may be adjustable over another. "
"Then go to the relevant model chapter."
msgstr "已经掌握数据和研究问题的读者不必线性阅读。可以先用研究设计章审查分析单元的边界、决策期限、管理控制范围、测量定义和比较对象资格规则。识别投入、合意产出和非合意产出是必要的，但还不充分：情境条件不会自动成为资源，内部交接不会自动成为最终产出，在一个计划期内固定的数量换一个期限可能可以调整。之后再进入相关模型章节。"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:97 07c49b4dc24d42c684d40719c6f29b7c
msgid ""
"After running the code, do not keep only one efficiency column. Comparator "
"organizations, benchmark operating plans, resource excesses, output "
"shortfalls, and returns to scale often explain the result better than "
"rankings do."
msgstr "运行代码后，不要只保留一列效率得分。比较对象、标杆经营方案、投入冗余、产出不足和规模报酬，往往比排名更能解释结果。"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:102 3915325de7bb40e590c422e9d00dcec4
msgid ""
"Most model chapters use small datasets as magnifying glasses for observing "
"model behavior. Before substituting your own data, reproduce the book's "
"result with its theory dataset; that simple step catches many errors "
"involving column roles, orientation, and score direction. The community-"
"hospital chapter then brings the main design and reporting choices together "
"in one larger synthetic study. It is a workflow template, not evidence about"
" a real health system. A publishable application must use defensible source "
"data, document provenance and units, screen its comparison population, pre-"
"specify sensitivity analyses, and report the limitations of its final "
"conclusions."
msgstr "多数模型章把小型数据集用作观察模型行为的放大镜。替换成自己的数据之前，请先用书中的理论数据重现结果；这一简单步骤能发现许多与列角色、导向和得分方向有关的错误。社区医院章随后在一个规模较大的合成研究中汇集主要设计与报告选择。它是一份工作流程模板，而不是关于真实医疗系统的证据。可发表的应用研究必须使用来源可信的数据，记录数据出处和单位，筛选比较总体，预先设定敏感性分析，并报告最终结论的局限。"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:112 5aae60b2d2804adeb70d4891d8e228e4
msgid "If You Compare or Develop Methods"
msgstr "如果你要比较或开发方法"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:114 9e15a546afc44aea9fe7a38926d9b97e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If you want to compare methods or develop a new model, keep {doc}`notation` "
"and the model map in the appendix close at hand. Start by separating the "
"management question, the operating system, the organizations and periods "
"supplying evidence, and the improvement or economic objective. Technology "
"assumptions and equations then make those choices precise. Historically "
"different names are combined when they lead to the same attainable plans and"
" performance criterion; genuine differences in production structure, "
"disposability, scale, benchmark policy, valuation, or statistical claim "
"remain visible."
msgstr ""
"如果你希望比较方法或开发新模型，请把 {doc}`notation` "
"和附录中的模型图放在手边。首先分开管理问题、经营系统、提供证据的组织与时期，以及改进目标或经济目标，再用技术假设和公式精确表达这些选择。历史名称不同、但导出相同可行方案和绩效准则的方法合并讲解；生产结构、可处置性、规模、标杆政策、价值评价或统计主张上的实质差异则清楚保留。"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:123 f7b0c0fcd7004b1f851a3a9cd20fdd11
msgid "Moving from a management problem to usable evidence"
msgstr "从管理问题走向可用证据"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:125 057eeabda23a47c8a7c85d16c5f9f9ac
msgid ""
"Each form of evidence in the book answers a different practical question. "
"The economic discussion identifies the responsibility being assessed: saving"
" resources, protecting services, improving environmental outcomes, or "
"raising productivity. Figures show whose experience supplies a credible "
"comparison and what operating change that comparison makes possible. "
"Equations state the assumptions precisely, while code tests whether the same"
" reasoning survives realistic combinations of resources, services, "
"organizations, and periods. When reading a diagram, ask first what "
"management can alter, what it must preserve, and whether the proposed "
"benchmark could be implemented within the stated horizon. Coordinates and "
"arrows are useful only insofar as they make those organizational choices "
"easier to see."
msgstr "本书中的不同证据回答不同的实践问题。经济讨论确定所评价的责任：节约资源、保护服务、改善环境结果或提高生产率。图形显示谁的经验构成可信比较，以及这种比较能够支持怎样的经营变化；公式精确陈述假设；代码则检验同一逻辑能否适用于资源、服务、组织和时期的现实组合。阅读图示时，先问管理者可以改变什么、必须保留什么，以及所提标杆能否在声明的期限内实施。坐标和箭头只有在帮助我们看清这些组织选择时才有价值。"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:136 112b90a2e7fa4349814c3232dcad8631
msgid ""
"Code blocks contain what is needed to understand and reproduce the analysis."
" Complete parameters, return fields, exceptions, and version-compatibility "
"details live in the separate DEAPack Documentation. The text asks why a "
"model is appropriate and what its result can support. Readers can consult "
"the API pages alongside an example when implementation detail is needed, "
"while the main argument remains readable without them."
msgstr ""
"代码块只保留理解和重现分析所需的内容。完整参数、返回字段、异常和版本兼容细节见单独的 DEAPack "
"文档。正文讨论模型为何适用、结果能够支持什么。需要实现细节时，读者可以在阅读示例的同时查询 API 页面，而主线论证即使脱离这些页面也应保持通畅。"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:143 ddab023baf87472080e4180ef384c278
msgid ""
"The handbook concentrates on mature model families that organize the field. "
"A paper-specific variant enters the main route only when it has become a "
"principal family and changes the production setting, performance criterion, "
"or interpretation in a way the existing family cannot express. Specialized "
"variants and computational options remain in the DEAPack Documentation."
msgstr ""
"本 Handbook "
"聚焦能够组织整个领域的成熟模型族。只有当某篇论文提出的变体已经成为主要方法族，并以现有方法族无法表达的方式改变生产环境、绩效准则或解释时，它才进入正文主线。专门化变体和计算选项保留在"
" DEAPack 文档中。"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:149 4c645717addc4e8b8439dc5d46df41fe
msgid "Numerical integrity without software plumbing"
msgstr "不让软件细节遮蔽数值完整性"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:151 fe46294ef71848499dd5c97afaee9071
msgid ""
"A performance number is informative only when the comparison it summarizes "
"actually exists. If another period's technology cannot support the required "
"appraisal, or a decomposition is undefined, it remains missing; it is never "
"replaced by zero or described as poor performance. The missing result marks "
"a limit of the evidence. Each model chapter therefore identifies the "
"feasibility and accounting conditions that must hold before the result can "
"inform a management or policy discussion."
msgstr "只有当得分所概括的比较确实存在时，绩效数值才有信息意义。如果另一时期的技术无法支持所需评价，或某项分解没有定义，结果就保持缺失；绝不能用零填补，也不能称为绩效不佳。缺失结果标示的是证据边界。因此，各模型章都会说明结果进入管理或政策讨论之前必须满足的可行性与核算条件。"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:159 59ea7f83f9cc495fa1499f510c4abd12
msgid ""
"DEAPack also retains field-level numerical diagnostics for readers who need "
"to audit a computation. Those diagnostic names, tolerances, and failure "
"statuses are described in the package Documentation. The handbook keeps the "
"substantive question in view: what has been established about the "
"organization's production possibilities, and what remains unsupported?"
msgstr ""
"DEAPack 还为需要审计计算过程的读者保留字段层面的数值诊断。诊断名称、容差和失败状态见包文档。Handbook "
"始终把实质问题置于中心：关于组织的生产可能性，我们究竟已经确认了什么，还有什么缺乏支持？"

#: ../../reading-guide.md:165 837535ad4d954f7e85f4ca224ee329f9
msgid ""
"One final habit is especially useful. Whenever a unit has an efficiency "
"score of one, ask: Efficient under which technology, orientation, period, "
"and peer group? That question runs through almost the entire book."
msgstr "最后请养成一个格外有用的习惯。每当某个单元的效率得分等于 1，都追问一句：它是在什么技术、导向、时期和比较群体下有效率？这个问题贯穿本书几乎所有章节。"
